														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1729727">
									

<p>How on earth is something that small able to eat someone? 150&#160;kg is very little, there's many humans bigger than that. Also, 15 meters is a gigantic distance from the lure. Plus, how does it even sense when people come near the lure? Insects don't technically have tongues, and it's unclear how this &quot;tongue&quot; is even strong enough to pull in a whole human. What's the mechanism for shaping the lure, and with enough precision (Including clothes!) to fool someone who knows the mimicked individual intimately? I don't buy that this thing can squish itself down to about 6 inches high, much less eat someone in that position. If this thing actually catches something, it's getting about half its mass in food. This doesn't seem like it would suggest the thing constantly trying to eat more and more.</p>
<p>Yes, you can explain all this with &quot;Well, it's anomalous!&quot;. But there's an awful lot of anomalies here, then. Enough that I can't buy this thing at all. It just doesn't make sense. On top of that, the journal entries are cliched and obvious, which would probably be enough for a downvote there.</p>

